          "0": {
            "id": "14060201",
            "headline": "Sembcorp is said to gauge demand for $394 million India unit IPO",
            "heading": "Sembcorp is said to gauge demand for $394 million India unit IPO",
            "intro": "The Temasek Holdings Pte.-backed renewable energy company is considering an IPO launch as early as December",
            "body": "Singapore-based Sembcorp Industries Ltd. is meeting investors for a proposed initial public offering of its Indian unit, Sembcorp Green Infra Ltd., that could raise as much as $394 million, according to people familiar with the matter.\r\n\r\nThe Temasek Holdings Pte.-backed renewable energy company is considering an IPO launch as early as December, the people said, asking not to be identified because the information is private.\r\n\r\nSembcorp Green Infra filed draft papers in August for an IPO comprising a fresh issue of shares worth as much as Rs 3,750 crore ($394 million) and is awaiting regulatory approval.\r\n\r\nDeliberations are ongoing and details of the offering, including its timing and size, could change, the people said. Representatives for Sembcorp didn\u2019t immediately respond to requests for comment.\r\n\r\nSembcorp is working with Axis Capital Ltd., Citigroup Inc., CLSA, HSBC Holdings Plc, ICICI Securities Ltd., IIFL Capital Services Ltd. and Kotak Mahindra Capital Co., the people said.\r\n\r\nIndia\u2019s primary market is gathering momentum with the record IPO of Jio Platforms Ltd., which was subscribed more than 22 times last week. Several companies are preparing to tap the market over the next two months. IPOs in the country have raised nearly $18 billion this year, putting the market on course to challenge last year\u2019s record of about $22.4 billion.\r\n\r\nSembcorp Green Infra is among India\u2019s 10 largest renewable independent power producers by operational capacity as of March 31, 2026, according to its IPO prospectus. The company has more than 75 renewable-energy assets across 18 states, with 7.6 gigawatts of gross renewable-energy capacity installed and under development in India.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/sembcorp-is-said-to-gauge-demand-for-394-million-india-unit-ipo-14060201.html",
