          "1": {
            "id": "14060127",
            "headline": "Coca-Cola India bottler likely to file DRHP this week for $1 billion IPO",
            "heading": "Coca-Cola India bottler likely to file DRHP this week for $1 billion IPO",
            "intro": "Hindustan Coca-Cola Holdings is likely to file its draft red herring prospectus for a $1 billion IPO this week, as per sources.",
            "body": "Hindustan Coca-Cola Holdings (HCCH), the parent company for Indian Coca Cola bottler Hindustan Coca-Cola Beverages, is likely to file its draft red herring prospectus (DRHP) with the market regulator this week, according to sources. The listing will likely occur in 2027.\r\n\r\nSome of the key investment bankers making up the issue's syndicate are Axis Capital and IIFL Capital Services, the same sources added. A report by Bloomberg suggested that the issue size could be around $1 billion, which would largely be a stake-sale, with the firm seeking valuation of $10 billion.\r\n\r\nThe company has retained Rothschild &amp;amp; Co to advise on the listing.\r\n\r\nIn July 2025, the Coca-Cola Company completed a transaction in which Jubilant Bhartia Group acquired a 40% stake in HCCH, while the firm retained 60%.\u00a0 &quot;The potential listing will be a significant milestone, completing the refranchising of HCCH and positioning it well to capitalize on the opportunities in the Indian market,&quot; said the company in a media statement.\r\n\r\n&quot;This announcement is another important step for HCCB,\u201d said Sanket Ray, president, India and Southwest Asia and Emerging Large Markets Lead for The Coca-Cola Company. \u201cUnder the leadership of our trusted partners in Jubilant Bhartia Group, following the listing the bottler will be well placed to continue to pursue growth.&quot;\r\n\r\nChairman and Co-Chairman of Jubilant Bhartia Group, Shyam and Hari Bhartia, added: \u201cWe are excited to take this next important step in the bottler\u2019s journey and reap the benefits of the public listing to create value for all shareholders. Equally, we are looking forward to continuing to work with The Coca-Cola Company, as an important shareholder in the company.\u201d\r\n\r\nEstablished in 1997, the bottler operates 14 bottling plants across 10 states and packages, distributes, and sells beverages, including Coca-Cola, Thums Up, Sprite, and Fanta. The firm operated a network of more than 2,000 distributors and reached over 1.7 million customers, thanks to its approximately 5,000 employees.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.\r\n\r\n&amp;nbsp;",
