          "2": {
            "id": "14060110",
            "headline": "EAAA India Alternatives IPO subscribed 5% so far on Day 1; check latest GMP",
            "heading": "EAAA India Alternatives IPO subscribed 5% so far on Day 1; check latest GMP",
            "intro": "The initial public offering (IPO) of EAAA India Alternatives opened for subscription on October 26, with the issue receiving 5% subscription by 12:30 pm on the first day of bidding, according to data from the National Stock Exchange (NSE).",
            "body": "The initial public offering (IPO) of EAAA India Alternatives opened for subscription on October 26, with the issue receiving 5% subscription by 12:30 pm on the first day of bidding, according to data from the National Stock Exchange (NSE).\r\n\r\nThe Rs 1,200-crore IPO received bids for 2,50,740 shares against 52,99,684 shares on offer.\r\n\r\nAmong investor categories, Qualified Institutional Buyers (QIBs) led the demand, subscribing to 8% of their allotted portion. The non-institutional investor (NII) category was subscribed 7%, while the retail portion received bids for 2% of the shares reserved for the category.\r\n\r\nRead Also:\u00a0From selling hair dye to Rs 2,000-crore 'Aachi Masala' brand: How Padmasingh Isaac took a family recipe from Chennai to the world\r\n\r\nIn the grey market, the EAAA India Alternatives IPO was commanding a grey market premium (GMP) of 2.19% on the morning of October 26, according to InvestorGain.\r\n\r\nThe grey market premium is an unofficial indicator of investor sentiment towards a public issue before its listing. However, it does not guarantee listing gains, and the premium can fluctuate depending on market conditions and investor demand.\r\n\r\nThe Rs 1,200-crore public issue will remain open for subscription from October 26 to October 28. The company has fixed the price band at Rs 1,585-1,665 per share.\r\n\r\nThe IPO is entirely an offer-for-sale (OFS), through which promoter entity Edelweiss Securities and Investments will sell its stake in the company.\r\n\r\nSince the issue comprises only an offer-for-sale, the company will not receive any proceeds from the IPO. The proceeds, excluding offer-related expenses, will go to the selling shareholder.\r\n\r\nAhead of the public issue, EAAA India Alternatives raised Rs 360 crore through its anchor book. The anchor investors included Government Pension Fund Global, Schroder International, Hornbill Capital Advisors, Goldman Sachs and BNP Paribas Financial Markets.\r\n\r\nAxis Capital, Jefferies India, Motilal Oswal Investment Advisors and Nuvama Wealth Management are acting as the merchant bankers to the issue.\r\n\r\nCheck IPO News Here\r\n\r\nEAAA India Alternatives operates primarily across two business verticals: real assets and private credit. It also offers portfolio management services and focuses on managing long-term capital.\r\n\r\nAs of June 2026, the company had assets under management (AUM) of Rs 95,344.8 crore.\r\n\r\nUnder its real assets business, the company invests in infrastructure and commercial real estate assets through a combination of equity, quasi-equity and debt instruments.\r\n\r\nIts private credit business provides credit and flexible financing solutions to borrowers. These investments allow the company to participate in alternative investment opportunities beyond traditional listed equity and debt markets.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
